edeem`"},"previewWithdrawRequest(uint256)":{"details":"Simulate the effects of a withdrawal request at the current block. Returns the amount of `shares` that would be burned if this entire withdrawal request were to be processed at the current block. Note: This is equivalent of EIP-4626 `previewWithdraw`"},"requestRedeem(uint256)":{"details":"Submits a withdrawal request, incurring a fee."},"serviceConfiguration()":{"details":"The ServiceConfiguration."},"settings()":{"details":"The current configurable pool settings."},"state()":{"details":"The current pool state."},"symbol()":{"details":"Returns the symbol of the token, usually a shorter version of the name."},"totalAvailableAssets()":{"details":"Calculate the total amount of underlying assets held by the vault, excluding any assets due for withdrawal."},"totalAvailableSupply()":{"details":"The total available supply that is not marked for withdrawal"},"totalSupply()":{"details":"See {IERC20-totalSupply}."},"transfer(address,uint256)":{"details":"See {IERC20-transfer}. Requirements: - `to` cannot be the zero address. - the caller must have a balance of at least `amount`."},"transferFrom(address,address,uint256)":{"details":"See {IERC20-transferFrom}. Emits an {Approval} event indicating the updated allowance. This is not required by the EIP. See the note at the beginning of {ERC20}. NOTE: Does not update the allowance if the current allowance is the maximum `uint256`. Requirements: - `from` and `to` cannot be the zero address. - `from` must have a balance of at least `amount`. - the caller must have allowance for ``from``'s tokens of at least `amount`."}},"stateVariables":{"_accountings":{"details":"Various accounting statistics updated throughout the pool lifetime."},"_liquidityAsset":{"details":"Reference to the underlying liquidity asset for the pool."},"_serviceConfiguration":{"details":"Reference to the global service configuration."},"activatedAt":{"details":"The activation timestamp of the pool."},"poolAcce